An empty PKI directory is the normal state of a fresh client, not a fault: a trust list holds
nothing until the user trusts a server, and a revocation list stays empty unless the operator
maintains CRLs. loadAllFilesInDirectory() nevertheless logs it at warning level and returns
success, so every single connect prints two warnings. They also name no path, which makes the
pair indistinguishable -- the reader cannot tell the trust list from the revocation list. Log
the expected case at debug level and say which directory it was.

diff --git a/src/plugins/opcua/open62541/qopen62541backend.cpp b/src/plugins/opcua/open62541/qopen62541backend.cpp
--- a/src/plugins/opcua/open62541/qopen62541backend.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/opcua/open62541/qopen62541backend.cpp
@@ -2166,7 +2166,8 @@ bool Open62541AsyncBackend::loadAllFilesInDirectory(const QString &location, UA_B
     auto entries = dir.entryList(QDir::Files);

     if (entries.isEmpty()) {
-        qCWarning(QT_OPCUA_PLUGINS_OPEN62541) << "Directory is empty";
+        // ouaexp patch: an empty trust or revocation list is expected, and the path identifies it
+        qCDebug(QT_OPCUA_PLUGINS_OPEN62541) << "No files to load in" << location;
         return true;
     }

